Statistics are collected for indexes built by a schema change, before that
schema change commits (see docs/design/atomic-index-stats.md).

Covers:
  - CREATE INDEX populates sqlite_stat1 with no explicit ANALYZE
  - those statistics are visible on every node, not just the master
  - ALTER TABLE adding an index does the same, without disturbing the
    statistics of indexes it did not rebuild
  - altering an index definition refreshes its statistics
  - a datacopy-driven rebuild does not lose existing statistics
  - DROP INDEX does not resurrect statistics
  - the analyze_new_indexes tunable disables the behavior

Runs standalone or against a cluster; the per-node checks degrade to a
single-host check when there is only one node.
